</div></div></div><div class="mantine-Timeline-item Timeline-module__Yc6Oca__item undefined mantine-1ct4i8l" data-active="true" data-current="true"><div class="mantine-15oosng mantine-Timeline-itemBullet" data-with-child="true" data-active="true"><div class="mantine-ThemeIcon-root Timeline-module__Yc6Oca__icon mantine-qg2s9c"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="2" y="6" width="20" height="8" rx="1"></rect><path d="M17 14v7"></path><path d="M7 14v7"></path><path d="M17 3v3"></path><path d="M7 3v3"></path><path d="M10 14 2.3 6.3"></path><path d="m14 6 7.7 7.7"></path><path d="m8 6 8 8"></path></svg></div></div><div class="mantine-480qv8 mantine-Timeline-itemBody"><div class="mantine-480qv8 mantine-Timeline-itemContent"><div class="Timeline-module__Yc6Oca__itemContent"><div class="h6 Timeline-module__Yc6Oca__itemTitle">Delivery and Construction</div><strong class="Timeline-module__Yc6Oca__footer">July 2026 - Q2 2028</strong></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="StickyBlock-module__tbS1eq__content"><div class=""><h2 class="h6 project-module__TWNZmq__title">Project Overview </h2><div class="gridLayout gridLayout__isContained Wysiwyg-module__VQKDKa__wrapper"><div class="Prose-module__IX6RXa__prose gridLayout"><p><span>1113-1125 Dundas Street West is a new rental housing development on City-owned land in Toronto’s Spadina-Fort York community, led by CreateTO as public builder. As the first CreateTO public builder project to break ground, the development marks an important milestone in a new City-led approach to delivering housing on public land.  </span></p><p><span>CreateTO, on behalf of the City of Toronto, is repurposing the site (formerly occupied by a Green P surface parking lot and a vacant, semi-detached home) to create 74 new rental homes, including at least 17 affordable homes. Designed to support a range of households, the development will include family-sized units in a vibrant, transit-oriented neighbourhood.  </span></p><p><span>By leveraging City-owned land and a City-led delivery model, the project demonstrates how the public sector can help create more housing, faster and efficiently, while supporting affordability and sustainability. The development reflects a collaborative effort between CreateTO and the City of Toronto to advance housing solutions that deliver lasting community benefit. </span></p><p><span>Sustainability has been a guiding principle of the project from the outset, as part of the Mass Timber Pilot Program launched by CreateTO and City partners. It explores how innovative, low-carbon construction methods can support faster, more sustainable housing delivery, the development incorporated sustainability at every stage.  </span></p><p><span>In preparation for redevelopment, the vacant home on the site at 1113 Dundas Street West was carefully deconstructed rather than demolished, allowing materials to be diverted from landfill and supporting a more circular approach to construction.  </span></p><p><span>The new building will incorporate mass timber construction, geothermal energy and other low-carbon design strategies to reduce environmental impacts and support a more sustainable community. </span></p><p><span>Construction is scheduled to begin in Summer 2026 and continue through 2027. </span></p><p>This project is supported in part through funding provided by the Government of Canada under Build Canada Homes, supporting the development of affordable and non-market housing.</p><h4><b>Key Project Facts</b></h4><ul><li><p><span>10-storey rental housing building </span></p></li><li><p><span>74 new rental homes, including at least 17 affordable homes and family-sized units </span></p></li><li><p><span>Mass timber construction and geothermal energy systems </span></p></li><li><p><span>78 bicycle parking spaces </span></p></li><li><p><span>Private resident amenity space </span></p></li></ul><h4>Key Project Milestones</h4><ul><li><p><b>2022</b>: CreateTO and City partners launch the Mass Timber Pilot Program. </p></li><li><p><b>2023/2024</b>: Community consultation and submission of an Official Plan and Zoning By-Law Amendment. </p></li><li><p><b>2024:</b> Planning approvals are secured for the development. </p></li><li><p><b>2025</b>: Site preparation begins, including the deconstruction of the existing vacant home. Check out a timelapse and deconstruction photos below. </p></li><li><p><b>Summer 2026:</b> Construction begins for CreateTO&#x27;s first public builder project. </p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#335A52">Have a question about the 1113 – 1125 Dundas Street West Mass Timber Pilot project or want to sign up for project updates? If so, email </span><a href="mailto:masstimber@createto.ca" target="_blank"><span style="color:#335A52"><u>masstimber@createto.ca</u></span></a><span style="color:#335A52"> </span></p><p><span style="color:#335A52"><i>Note: The address for this project is 1113-1125 Dundas Street West, but the site is commonly referred to as 1113-1117 Dundas Street West.</i></span><span style="color:#335A52"> </span></p></div><div class="gridLayout WysiwygBlock-module__eqBvbG__wrapper WysiwygBlock-module__eqBvbG__wrapper__isSizeFeatured"></div><div class="gridLayout WysiwygBlock-module__eqBvbG__wrapper WysiwygBlock-module__eqBvbG__wrapper__isSizeContainer"><div id="_R_ud3kr6_" class="Gallery-module__p5_gjG__wrapper Gallery-module__p5_gjG__wrapper__isSlider"><h2 class="visuallyHidden">Media Gallery</h2><div class="Gallery-module__p5_gjG__inner"><div class="Gallery-module__p5_gjG__controls"><button class="IconAction-module__LaarvW__wrapper IconAction-module__LaarvW__wrapper__isSecondary IconAction-module__LaarvW__wrapper__isSizeMd Gallery-module__p5_gjG__control js-prev" type="button"><span class="visuallyHidden">Previous</span><svg aria-hidden="true" class="Icon