ow home to many diverse First Nations, Inuit and Métis peoples.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Learn more","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/about-us/land-acknowledgement","uuid":"8f58303c-9775-46e6-a357-12f863a43c78","anchor":null,"target":"_self","linktype":"story","story":{"name":"Land Acknowledgement","id":481725,"uuid":"8f58303c-9775-46e6-a357-12f863a43c78","slug":"land-acknowledgement","url":"about-us/land-acknowledgement","full_slug":"about-us/land-acknowledgement","_stopResolving":true}}}]}]}]}},"articles":[{"externalSource":null,"id":"8fe13500-707d-4c76-855b-5ca090e05329","href":"https://www.toronto.ca/news/city-of-toronto-breaks-ground-on-74-new-sustainable-rental-homes-in-trinity-bellwoods/","initiatives":["a22c3ccc-cfc0-48c9-800d-345fc4ed58af"],"isExternal":true,"title":"City of Toronto breaks ground on 74 new sustainable rental homes in Trinity-Bellwoods","createdAt":"2026-08-24T17:59:54.360Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-24T18:02:20.722Z","excerpt":"","tags":[],"image":{"src":"https://a-us.storyblok.com/f/1017201/3600x2401/b18bb8cd56/createto_082426_0889-1113-dundas-groundbreaking.jpg","alt":"","title":"","focus":"1296x987:1297x988"}},{"externalSource":null,"id":"e7e3ca22-82d9-4baa-8717-60d594f2bfb9","href":"https://canada.constructconnect.com/dcn/news/infrastructure/2023/05/createto-embarks-on-10-storey-mass-timber-pilot-project","initiatives":["7ece5bec-2963-4f33-99ac-55ae45e0ea5d"],"isExternal":true,"title":"CreateTO embarks on 10-storey mass timber pilot project","createdAt":"2023-05-15T07:00:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2023-12-19T18:14:08.444Z","excerpt":"When a 10-storey residence rises near Trinity Bellwoods Park on Dundas Street West in Toronto next year, it will mark CreateTO’s first foray into the mass timber world.","tags":[],"image":{"src":"https://a-us.storyblok.com/f/1017201/1024x576/7b7fda21d3/dp-create-to-57bd4db2-38ef-4f60-8eef-d0b78053ac2f-mainweb.jpg","alt":"Mass Timber","title":"","focus":""}},{"externalSource":null,"id":"dcb69684-b945-44be-97ca-cdc3c89905d8","href":"https://www.thestar.com/news/gta/city-plans-to-turn-parking-lot-into-affordable-housing-made-of-mass-timber/article_2412ba3f-6f56-5e37-ac1a-b7a2fa74da11.html","initiatives":["a22c3ccc-cfc0-48c9-800d-345fc4ed58af","7ece5bec-2963-4f33-99ac-55ae45e0ea5d"],"isExternal":true,"title":"City plans to turn parking lot into affordable housing made of mass timber","createdAt":"2022-04-26T07:00:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2023-12-19T18:35:36.392Z","excerpt":"A proposed new mass timber housing development, slated for what is now a surface-level Green P parking lot in Toronto’s downtown west area, will address affordability issues and climate concerns.","tags":[],"image":{"src":"https://a-us.storyblok.com/f/1017201/1200x800/162f9346ed/645a644a1ff29-image.jpg","alt":"Mass Timber","title":"","focus":""}},{"externalSource":null,"id":"d30843c3-208d-4e45-93c3-17eeaaf19c09","href":"https://www.toronto.ca/news/mayor-john-tory-announces-new-mass-timber-pilot-program-for-affordable-rental-housing/","initiatives":["a22c3ccc-cfc0-48c9-800d-345fc4ed58af","7ece5bec-2963-4f33-99ac-55ae45e0ea5d"],"isExternal":true,"title":"Mayor John Tory announces new mass timber pilot program for affordable rental housing","createdAt":"2022-04-25T07:00:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2023-12-05T16:53:48.484Z","excerpt":"Today, Mayor John Tory, joined by Deputy Mayor Ana Bailão (Davenport), Chair, Planning and Housing Committee and Councillor Joe Cressy (Spadina-Fort York) announced a pilot program that will bring new affordable rental housing to the City-owned site at 1113-1117 Dundas St. W.","tags":[],"image":{"src":"https://a-us.storyblok.com/f/1015016/1280x720/b042a9b4a1/masstimberannouncement.jpg","alt":"","title":"","focus":""}}],"activeBlock":null,"canonicalUrl":"/projects/1113-1117-dundas-street-west","page":{"name":"1113-1117 Dundas Street West","created_at":"2023-10-26T17:45:31.405Z","published_at":"2026-08-21T15:29:12.222Z","updated_at":"2026-08-21T15:29:12.256Z","id":481853,"uuid":"8156878d-c5e5-4f40-9bc0-043bbc425705","content":{"_uid":"21c3b6fa-0554-4001-89e3-7b4d317fceaf","body":{"type":"doc","attrs":{"backgroundColor":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"1113-1125 Dundas Street West is a new rental housing development on City-owned land in Toronto’s Spadina-Fort York community, led by CreateTO as public builder. As the first CreateTO public builder project to break ground, the development marks an important milestone in a new City-led approach to delivering housing on public land.  ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":""}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":"left"},"content":[{"text":"CreateTO, on behalf of the City of Toronto, is repurposing the site (formerly occupied by a Green P surface parking lot and a vacant, semi-detached home) to create 74 new rental homes, including at least 17 affordable homes. Designed to support a range of households, the development will include family-sized units in a vibrant, transit-oriented neighbourhood.  ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":""}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":"left"},"content":[{"text":"By leveraging City-owned land and a City-led delivery model, the project demonstrates how the public sector can help create more housing, faster and efficiently, while supporting affordability and sustainability. The development reflects a collaborative effort between CreateTO and the City of Toronto to advance housing solutions that deliver lasting community benefit. ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":""}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":"left"},"content":[{"text":"Sustainability has been a guiding principle of the project from the outset, as part of the Mass Timber Pilot Program launched by CreateTO and City partners. It explores how innovative, low-carbon construction methods can support faster, more sustainable housing delivery, the development incorporated sustainability at every stage.  ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":""}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":"left"},"content":[{"text":"In preparation for redevelopment, the vacant home on the site at 1113 Dundas Street West was carefully deconstructed rather than demolished, allowing materials to be diverted from landfill and supporting a more circular approach to construction.  ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":""}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":"left"},"content":[{"text":"The new building will incorporate mass timber construction, geothermal energy and other low-carbon design strategies to reduce environmental impacts and support a more sustainable community. ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":""}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":"left"},"content":[{"text":"Construction is scheduled to begin in Summer 2026 and continue through 2027. ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":""}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":"left"},"content":[{"text":"This project is supported in part through funding provided by the Government of Canada under Build Canada Homes, supporting the development of affordable and non-market housing.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4,"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Key Project Facts","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":""}},{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"bullet_list","content":[{"type":"list_item","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"10-storey rental housing building ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":""}}]}]}]},{"type":"list_item","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"74 new rental homes, including at least 17 affordable homes and family-sized units ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":""}}]}]}]},{"type":"list_item","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Mass timber construction and geothermal energy systems ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":""}}]}]}]},{"type":"list_item","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"78 bicycle parking spaces ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":""}}]}]}]},{"type":"list_item","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Private resident amenity space ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":""}}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":4,"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Key Project Milestones","type":"text"}]},{"type":"bullet_list","content":[{"type":"list_item","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"2022","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"text":": CreateTO and City partners launch the Mass Timber Pilot Program. ","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"list_item","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"2023/2024","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"text":": Community consultation and submission of an Official Plan and Zoning By-Law Amendment. ","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"list_item","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"2024:","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"text":" Planning approvals are secured for the development. ","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"list_item","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"2025","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"text":": Site preparation begins, including the deconstruction of the existing vacant home. Check out a timelapse and deconstruction photos below. ","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"list_item","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Summer 2026:","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"text":" Construction begins for CreateTO's first public builder project. ","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Have a question about the 1113 – 1125 Dundas Street West Mass Timber Pilot project or want to sign up for project updates? If so, email ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#335A52"}}]},{"text":"masstimber@createto.ca","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"mailto:masstimber@createto.ca","uuid":null,"anchor":null,"target":"_blank","linktype":"url"}},{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#335A52"}},{"type":"underline"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#335A52"}}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"text":"Note: The address for this project is 1113-1125 Dundas Street West, but the site is commonly referred to as 1113-1117 Dundas Street West.","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#335A52"}},{"type":"italic"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"textStyle","attrs":{"color":"#335A52"}}]}]},{"type":"blok","attrs":{"id":"89bbde30-8e71-4711-8923-f445a9ad6471","body":[{"_uid":"i-048905ee-170b-489f-af5c-dd651825bfc2","video":{"id":null,"alt":null,"name":"","focus":null,"title":null,"source":null,"filename":"","copyright":null,"fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{}},"tracks":[],"component":"video","youtubeEmbed":"https://youtu.be/4WAwtkJnZbg"}]}},{"type":"blok","attrs":{"id":"512d9775-6e17-497f-9339-4497e28a6f48","body":[{"_uid":"i-77a598dc-deb0-4f02-86ba-d84f8910e805","images":[{"id":86547215287988,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a-us.storyblok.com/f/1017201/1920x1280/c10eac3059/deconstruction-gif.gif","copyright":"","fieldtype":"asset","meta_data":{}},{"id":86547557422786,"alt":"","name":"","focus":"","title":"","source":"","filename":"https://a-us.storyblok.com/f/1017201/1153x1728/12256fd39f/mass-timber-deconstruction-9.j